/-!
# The Eisenstein factors of the standard Lubin–Tate polynomial, and the division points

For the *standard* Lubin–Tate polynomial `f(T) = π T + T ^ q` (Milne, *CFT*, Example 2.10(a)) the
iterates `f^{(n)}` factor as

`f^{(n)}(T) = f^{[0]}(T) · f^{[1]}(T) · ⋯ · f^{[n]}(T)`,   `f^{[0]}(T) = T`,   `f^{[n]}(T) = f^{(n-1)}(T)^{q-1} + π`,

each `f^{[n]}` being monic of degree `(q-1)q^{n-1}` and Eisenstein at `π` (Milne, *CFT*, §I.3,
Remark 3.1).  The *division points* of the standard Lubin–Tate group are the roots of these
iterates,

`Λ_n = { x : f^{(n)}(x) = 0 } ⊆ F̄`,

and the Lubin–Tate level is `K_n = F(Λ_n)` (Milne, *op. cit.*, §I.3).

This file introduces

* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LTpolyEis` — the Eisenstein factor
  `f^{[n]}(T) = f^{(n-1)}(T)^{q-1} + π` of the iterate `f^{(n)}` (so that
  `LTpolyEis π q 0 = LTpolyFactor π q`);
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.badOrbit` — the orbit of the polynomial `ψ(c) = c(c+π)^{q-1}`
  used to show that no division point is a critical point of `f` (`q y^{q-1} + π ≠ 0` for
  `y ∈ Λ_n`), which is the key step in the separability of the iterates;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LTdivisionSet` — the set `Λ_n` of `π^n`-division points;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LTLevel` — the Lubin–Tate level `K_n = F(Λ_n)`, as an
  intermediate field of a fixed algebraic closure.

## Main definitions

* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LTpolyEis`;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.badOrbit`;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LTdivisionSet`;
* `NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate.LTLevel`.
-/

namespace NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate

universe u

noncomputable section

open Polynomial

/-- The **`n`-th Eisenstein factor** of the standard Lubin–Tate polynomial `f(T) = πT + T^q`:
the polynomial `f^{[n]}(T) = f^{(n-1)}(T)^{q-1} + π` such that `f^{(n)} = f^{[n]} · f^{(n-1)}`
(Milne, *CFT*, §I.3, Remark 3.1).  It is monic of degree `(q-1)q^{n-1}` and Eisenstein at `π`.

For `n = 0` it is the factor `LTpolyFactor π q = X^{q-1} + π` of `f` itself. -/
def LTpolyEis {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (π : A) (q n : ℕ) : Polynomial A :=
  (LTpolyIter π q n) ^ (q - 1) + Polynomial.C π

@[simp]
theorem LTpolyEis_zero {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (π : A) (q : ℕ) :
    LTpolyEis π q 0 = LTpolyFactor π q := rfl

/-- The **critical-point orbit** of the standard Lubin–Tate polynomial: the sequence
`c_0 = c`, `c_{j+1} = c_j (c_j + π)^{q-1}`.

The relevance is the identity `(f(y))^{q-1} = y^{q-1}(y^{q-1}+π)^{q-1}`: for a point `y` with
`y^{q-1} = c` the `(q-1)`-st powers of the orbit `y, f(y), f(f(y)), …` are the elements of
`badOrbit π q c`.  Since `f(y) = 0` forces `(f(y))^{q-1} = 0` (for `q ≥ 2`), a division point `y`
with `y^{q-1} = -π/q` — i.e. a critical point `f'(y) = 0` of `f` — would force
`badOrbit π q (-π/q) n = 0` at the level `n` at which `y` occurs. -/
def badOrbit {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (π : A) (q : ℕ) : A → ℕ → A
  | c, 0 => c
  | c, n + 1 => badOrbit π q c n * (badOrbit π q c n + π) ^ (q - 1)

@[simp]
theorem badOrbit_zero {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (π : A) (q : ℕ) (c : A) :
    badOrbit π q c 0 = c := rfl

@[simp]
theorem badOrbit_succ {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (π : A) (q n : ℕ) (c : A) :
    badOrbit π q c (n + 1) = badOrbit π q c n * (badOrbit π q c n + π) ^ (q - 1) := rfl

/-- The **`π^n`-division points** of the standard Lubin–Tate group of the series
`f(T) = πT + T^q`: the set `Λ_n` of roots in the algebraic closure of `F` of the iterate
`f^{(n)}` (Milne, *CFT*, §I.3).  For `n = 0` this is `{0}`.

In the classical theory `Λ_n` is the kernel of `[π^n]` on the Lubin–Tate module and is a free
`𝒪[F]/π^n`-module of rank one, hence has `q^n` elements (Milne, *op. cit.*, Theorem I.3.1). -/
def LTdivisionSet (F : Type u) [Field F] (π : F) (q n : ℕ) : Set (AlgebraicClosure F) :=
  (LTpolyIter π q n).rootSet (AlgebraicClosure F)

theorem LTpolyIter_ne_zero {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [Nontrivial A] (π : A) (q : ℕ) (n : ℕ)
    (hq : 2 ≤ q) : LTpolyIter π q n ≠ 0 :=
  (LubinTate.LTpolyIter_monic_degree π q n hq).1.ne_zero

theorem mem_LTdivisionSet_iff {F : Type u} [Field F] (π : F) (q n : ℕ) (hq : 2 ≤ q)
    {x : AlgebraicClosure F} :
    x ∈ LTdivisionSet F π q n ↔ (aeval x) (LTpolyIter π q n) = 0 := by
  rw [LTdivisionSet, Polynomial.mem_rootSet_of_ne (LTpolyIter_ne_zero π q n hq)]

/-- The **Lubin–Tate level** `K_n = F(Λ_n)`: the subfield of a fixed algebraic closure of `F`
generated by the `π^n`-division points (Milne, *CFT*, §I.3).  Classically `K_n/F` is totally
ramified abelian of degree `(q-1)q^{n-1}` and `Gal(K_n/F) ≅ (𝒪[F]/π^n)^×`. -/
def LTLevel (F : Type u) [Field F] (π : F) (q n : ℕ) : IntermediateField F (AlgebraicClosure F) :=
  IntermediateField.adjoin F (LTdivisionSet F π q n)

theorem LTdivisionSet_subset_LTLevel (F : Type u) [Field F] (π : F) (q n : ℕ) :
    LTdivisionSet F π q n ⊆ (LTLevel F π q n : Set (AlgebraicClosure F)) :=
  IntermediateField.subset_adjoin F _

end

end NK.LocalReciprocityLubinTate
